			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1419873">
									

<p>Thing is, if he uses it his whole life, he's not aging, right? So when it goes under the sofa, why does he dislocate his arm and die rather than take the time to move the couch? I would ask how he got old if he has this thing, but I think the area of effect is poorly calibrated. How would you even notice that you weren't aging if you were just playing with this thing? The problem with the human strength thing is that it's /unscientific/- &quot;realistic limits&quot; is a very subjective term and these are supposed to be lab documents. It's a tone issue and that's not the only place where you go off track.</p>

