														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1419836">
									

<p>The Antikythera Mechanism isn't &quot;vaguely SCP-ish&quot;, unless you're one of the folks who cling tightly to the &quot;people that long ago CAN'T HAVE DONE THIS because they were that long ago&quot; style of thinking. This is the same path that, taken to an extreme, leads to the &quot;Aliens built the pyramids because obviously people in ancient Egypt can't have had any level of dedication or precision in their work&quot; mindset. We know what it is, we know how it works, we know what it's supposed to do, it was just the exact method of its construction that was lost to time. It's a case of &quot;Holy crap they were better at this than we thought,&quot; not &quot;OMG guyz ROMAN MECHANICAL MAGIC!&quot;</p>
<p>That said, I don't have an issue with this thing being old, or relating to an actual semi-mysterious thing, but this has *nothing* to do with the AM, nor does that actually seem to have any impact on the object's current status; you may as well have a chunk of stone from the construction of the Leaning Tower of Pisa to which someone later glued a resin gargoyle novelty statue, and changed &quot;As long as it's spun&quot; into &quot;As long as the block is balanced on one's head&quot;.</p>
<p>The object itself is&#8230; Decent, I guess is the best word I have for it, but I agree that the particulars of that really don't add at all to the item.</p>

							</div>

								
					
